    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d162">

                <pb facs="0232" n="130" xml:id="pg130"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/349: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">McMillin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-12-06T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            midnight.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Strictly confidential. Department’s December 4, 6.00 p.m.<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d162-f1"/> President Pardo received statement of President Wilson
                    with evident pleasure and satisfaction. He believes publication of statement
                    would have most beneficial effect and desires to know if there is any objection
                    to it being given to Peruvian press. Please expedite reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McMillin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
